WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.171
Welcome to the public DAJC demo.

00:00:02.451 --> 00:00:07.385
In this walkthrough, we will follow a transport from the overview
to its documents.

00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:09.825
All the data you see is synthetic.

00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:14.087
The opening screen shows active transports and their readiness.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:19.127
Look for warnings about missing documents, permits and
participant confirmations.

00:00:19.407 --> 00:00:26.768
The purpose of this overview is to help the dispatcher identify
which transport needs attention, and decide what to resolve next.

00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:29.877
Open D-ID Orders in the menu.

00:00:30.157 --> 00:00:34.685
Each row has its own identity, route, status and readiness
indicator.

00:00:34.965 --> 00:00:39.945
Select the first example: a gas turbine travelling from Ostrava
to Hamburg.

00:00:40.225 --> 00:00:44.231
Think of D-ID as a shared folder for one transport.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:48.447
Participants, documents and changes all belong to the same
assignment.

00:00:48.727 --> 00:00:55.275
This keeps the context together, instead of asking the dispatcher
to reconstruct it from separate messages.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:59.429
Inside the transport, start with Command Center.

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:05.154
Here you can review progress, planned milestones and the
readiness of individual steps.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:10.832
Warnings highlight issues such as missing permits or an escort
participant who has not yet confirmed.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:15.884
Check what is blocking progress and who needs to confirm the next
step.

00:01:16.164 --> 00:01:19.659
A readiness percentage is not official permission to travel.

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:24.629
The actual permits, approved route and transport conditions still
apply.

00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:27.982
Finally, open the Documents tab.

00:01:28.262 --> 00:01:31.385
Compare each document status and its versions.

00:01:31.665 --> 00:01:35.044
Approved indicates a document marked as approved in this demo.

00:01:35.324 --> 00:01:38.714
Required identifies a document that is still missing.

00:01:38.994 --> 00:01:44.868
Keeping these records with the same transport helps you see what
is ready and what needs attention.

00:01:45.148 --> 00:01:49.479
You can now explore the public demo yourself, using test data
only.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:57.619
To express interest in testing from the fourth of January, twenty
twenty seven, use the testing registration page on this website.